+GitHub has a built-in read surface, and it is a reader rather than a second forge. Single PR and issue reads are URL schemes resolved by the `read` tool, not by a forge client: `pr://<n>` for one PR, `pr://<n>/diff` for its changed files, `pr://<n>/diff/<i>` for one file's slice, `pr://<n>/diff/all` for the full unified diff, and `issue://<n>` for an issue or a PR's body, comments, and reviews. The same selectors take `<owner>/<repo>/` in front of the number to reach another repository, so `pr://<owner>/<repo>/<n>` names one PR elsewhere rather than listing anything. A separate `github` tool covers repository and file reads, search, PR create, PR checkout, PR push, and Actions run watching; it is gated behind `github.enabled`, which is off by default, and it exists only when `gh` is on `PATH`. Read each surface's doc before the first call in a session rather than assuming a form is valid because it parses.
